<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osaka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osaka is one of the largest cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and the centre of the Kansai region, at the mouth of the Yodo river on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka-bay">Osaka Bay</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka-castle">Osaka Castle</a> there from 1583 on the site of the Ishiyama Hongan-ji temple-fortress, and after the Tokugawa destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-clan">Toyotomi</a> in 1615 the city became the nation's great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> market and commercial hub. It remains a major centre of trade and industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osaka.jpg" alt="Osaka" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 663highland · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osaka_Castle_03bs3200.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
